  "description": "#514, the Edit-first order: one deny, not two. Sessions A and B read v1 and B commits v2, which makes A's copy INVALID. A's first call after the commit is an Edit, denied with the commit text. A's next Read, of the v2 bytes, is admitted at v2: the Edit's deny is the one A was told to read again after, so its Read is not denied a second time.",
